# [Perf] [AMD] quark: Pad W4A4 MXFP4 MoE to 128 columns for AITER FlyDSL
# https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/49852  (PR head cfc5974f72; this is its commit 1, 624fa95a85)
# Generated against the 20261117 image's SGLang checkout (c67db7c762) with patches 01-07, 09, 11 and 13 applied; source
# files only (tests dropped).
# Differs from the PR: behind the opt-in SGLANG_AMD_MXFP4_PAD128=1, so the TP1 MXFP4 MoE intermediate stays 640 wide
# (a multiple of 128) instead of being padded to 768; never set at the monokernel points.
# On the 20261117 image's AITER (581579ab; its fused-MoE configs equal v0.1.29's) the premise holds: gfx950 tuned FlyDSL
# rows exist at inter 640 for the fused shared expert (513 experts, top-k 11, tokens 1-16384, model_configs/
# qwen3_8_flash_fp4_tuned_fmoe.csv:2-16) and none at 768. ROCm/aiter#5757 (581579ab itself) adds asm rows at inter 160
# and 320 only, which neither padding reaches.
# Port from the 20261102 image (SGLang 1ced9a9eb0): the code is unchanged; only its context moved (sglang#49189 rewrote
# get_moe_padding_size, sglang#49660 moved _swizzle_mxfp4 to where the gate's helpers are inserted).
# Apply in /sgl-workspace/sglang with git apply.

